{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a distal C-H functionalization of electron-rich alkoxyarenes using organic photoredox catalysis. The method utilizes a radical-radical coupling strategy between a transient cyclohexadienyl radical (formed by azole addition to an arene radical cation) and various persistent radicals. This approach enables complete meta-regioselectivity for introducing alkoxycarbonyl, sulfonyl, pyridyl, and alkyl groups, providing a complementary alternative to traditional Friedel-Crafts reactions.",
